      {"t":"fill","q":"Lawv __ haus dej.","p":"They're drinking water.","a":["tab tom"],"o":["lawm","mam li","tsis tau"],"why":"tab tom (in the middle of) goes before the verb."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Kuv __ mus tsev.","p":"I'm going home.","a":["yuav"],"o":["lawm","tau","nyuam qhuav"],"why":"yuav before the verb points to what is coming."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I've eaten (use lawm only)","a":["Kuv noj mov lawm"],"hint":"noj mov (eat) · the 'done' word","x":["lawv"],"why":"lawm, with the tone letter m (the creaky tone), follows noj mov; lawv means they."},
      {"t":"type","p":"(use tab tom) They're drinking water","a":["Lawv tab tom haus dej"],"hint":"lawv (they) · haus dej (drink water) · in the middle of","x":["lawm","dev"],"why":"lawv (they) has the tone letter v (the rising tone); lawm is the 'done' word."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I will buy a book","a":["Kuv yuav yuav ib phau ntawv"],"hint":"yuav (will; buy) · ntawv (book)","x":["daim","phauj"],"why":"Books take the classifier phau; yuav comes twice, 'will' then 'buy'. phauj is an aunt."}
