      {"t":"fill","q":"Kuv mus __ khw.","p":"I'm going to the market.","a":["tom"],"o":["tob","saum","haus"],"why":"tom (over there, at) comes before the place."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Phau ntawv nyob __ lub rooj.","p":"The book is on the table.","a":["saum"],"o":["sau","hauv","nram"],"why":"saum is on top of; sau, with no m, means write."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I'm in the house","a":["Kuv nyob hauv lub tsev"],"hint":"nyob (be at) · hauv (in) · tsev (house)","x":["haus"],"why":"hauv ends in the tone letter v; haus means drink. Houses take lub."},
      {"t":"type","p":"The book is on the table","a":["Phau ntawv nyob saum lub rooj"],"hint":"ntawv (book) · nyob · saum (on top of) · rooj (table)","x":["daim","yog","nyom"],"why":"Books take phau and tables lub; location uses nyob, with the high tone letter b (nyom is grass)."},
      {"t":"type","p":"He's over there (the short form of tom)","a":["Nws nyob tod"],"hint":"nws · nyob · tom at the end of a phrase","x":["tob"],"why":"At the end of a phrase tom becomes tod, with the tone letter d."}
